    "cons": [
      "Listed at 78 dB at 50% load, the loudest here",
      "15,000 is the peak figure, not running watts"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The generator most people shopping for 20,000 watts should actually buy. It fills a 50-amp inlet for less money and much less weight.",
    "description": "The XP15000HX is here because most people searching for a 20,000-watt generator will connect it through a 50-amp inlet, and a 50-amp, 240V circuit tops out at 12,000 watts. DuroMax rates this unit at exactly 12,000 running and 15,000 peak watts on gasoline, and 11,400 running on propane, from a 670cc engine. The panel has a 14-50R, an L14-30R, an L5-30R and a row of 5-20R receptacles, and the 13.2-gallon tank is rated for 17.9 hours at 25% load or 12 hours at 50%. Push-button, remote and recoil starting are all available, and DuroMax lists a 5-year warranty. At 345 pounds dry it is still heavy, but it is about 200 pounds lighter than the Westinghouse. It is also the loudest unit here, listed at 78 dB at 50% load, so site it carefully. Unless your electrician is installing a 100-amp generator inlet, this is the sensible ceiling."
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best 20000 Watt Generators",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-20000-watt-generator/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a 20,000-watt generator enough to run a whole house?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most houses, yes, including central air, a well pump and an electric range at the same time. The catch is the connection: through a standard 50-amp inlet, only 12,000 watts reach the panel. To use the full output, you need a 100-amp inlet or transfer switch installed by an electrician."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much fuel does a 20,000-watt generator use?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Based on manufacturer runtime ratings, roughly 1.2 gallons an hour at quarter load and about 2 gallons an hour at half load for an open-frame 20kW unit. The DuroMax XP28000iH inverter works out to about 0.8 gallons an hour at quarter load. Over a full day of running, plan on 25 to 50 gallons."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a 20,000-watt generator weigh?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Between about 440 and 560 pounds dry. Westinghouse lists the WGen20000c at 541 pounds and the tri-fuel WGen20000TFc at 557. The DuroMax XP28000iH is 466 and the Generac GP18000EFI is 442.8. A full tank adds close to 100 pounds."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between 20,000 running and 20,000 peak watts?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Running watts are what the generator can carry continuously. Peak watts are a brief surge for starting motors. A 20,000-peak generator is often a 15,000 to 16,000-running generator. The Westinghouse WGen20000 models are rated at 20,000 running and 28,000 peak, so they are true 20kW units."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I plug a 20,000-watt generator into my house?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only through a transfer switch or a code-compliant interlock kit with an inlet box, installed by a licensed electrician. Never backfeed through a dryer outlet. For the full 20,000 watts, the connection must be rated for 100 amps or more, which usually means a terminal-block or hardwired hookup."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a 20,000-watt portable cheaper than a standby generator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The generator itself is usually cheaper. Once you add a 100-amp transfer switch, a gas connection and a permanent pad, the total installed cost often comes close to a 20 to 22kW air-cooled standby, which starts automatically and does not need refueling."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the quietest 20,000-watt generator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Of the units here, the DuroMax XP28000iH inverter has the lowest listed rating at 70 dB at 25% load. The Westinghouse open-frame models are listed at 74 dBA. All of them are louder than a typical home standby, so put them at least 20 feet from the house and away from bedroom windows."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Home Emergency Preparedness",
    tags: [
      "20000 watt generator",
      "generator 20000 watt",
      "20kw portable generator",
      "20000 watt portable generator",
      "largest home backup generator"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Updated November 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          The Best <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">20,000 Watt</span> Generators
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Only a few portables make a true 20,000 running watts. Here they are, plus the connection limit that decides whether you can use that power.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#westinghouse-wgen20000c"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            See the 5 Picks
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Alex Rivers</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Home Improvement Editor</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="6.2k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#watts-explained" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. What 20,000 Watts Means</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Our 5 Picks</a>
          <a href="#fifty-amp-ceiling" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. The 50-Amp Inlet Ceiling</a>
          <a href="#weight" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Living With 500 Pounds</a>
          <a href="#fuel" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Fuel Burn</a>
          <a href="#propane" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Propane and Natural Gas</a>
          <a href="#standby" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. When Standby Wins</a>
          <a href="#sizing" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Do You Need 20kW?</a>
          <a href="#inverter-or-open-frame" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Inverter or Open Frame</a>
          <a href="#placement" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Placement and Safety</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">12. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          A 20,000-watt portable is the largest generator most people can buy without a contractor, and it is easy to buy the wrong one. Many units sold at this size make 20,000 watts only as a starting surge, every one weighs as much as a refrigerator, and a standard 50-amp cord delivers just 12,000 watts to your panel. Below are the five that earn their size, and an honest account of when a 20kW standby is the better buy.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="watts-explained" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What "20,000 Watts" Actually Means on the Box
          </h2>

          <p>
            The biggest number on a large portable's box is almost always the peak or starting rating: the surge the alternator can hold for a second or two while a motor comes up to speed. The number you size a house around is the running rating, and on most generators marketed as 20,000-watt it is 25 to 40% lower. DuroMax's XP15000HX, for example, is a 15,000-watt generator on the box and a 12,000-watt generator once anything is actually running. Generac's GP18000EFI is sold on 22,500 starting watts and rated for 18,000 running.
          </p>

          <p>
            Only a handful of portables carry a true 20,000 running watts. The Westinghouse WGen20000c and WGen20000TFc are rated at 20,000 running and 28,000 peak on gasoline, and the DuroMax XP28000iH goes to 22,000 running. Everything else with a 20,000 near its name is a 15,000 to 18,000-watt machine counted at peak. That is not a scam, but it does mean two generators with similar headlines can differ by 8,000 running watts.
          </p>

          <p>
            Fuel changes the number too. Propane holds less energy per cubic foot than gasoline, so most dual and tri-fuel units are derated by 5 to 10% on propane and about 20% on natural gas. The WGen20000TFc is rated at 20,000 running watts on gasoline, 18,000 on propane and 16,000 on natural gas. If natural gas is the reason you are buying, 16,000 is the figure to plan around.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">THE RULE</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Size to running watts on the fuel you will actually use.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">Peak watts tell you whether a big motor will start. Running watts on your fuel tell you what the generator can carry once it has. Write both down for every model you compare.</p>
          </div>

          <p>
            To check your own load, add up the running watts of everything that has to run at once, then add the single largest starting surge on top. Our <a href="/generator-wattage-chart/">generator wattage chart</a> lists typical figures. A house with central air, a well pump and an electric range regularly comes in between 14,000 and 18,000 running watts, and that is the house this class of generator exists for.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Our 5 Top Picks Reviewed
          </h2>

          <p>
            Specs below come from the manufacturers' published ratings; owner reports are noted where they add something. Four of the five are true 18kW-plus running machines, and the fifth is the 12kW unit that suits most people better.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                    <span class="bg-[#FF4500] text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-black">
                      {index + 1}
                    </span>
                    {productImages[product.id] && (
                      <img
                        src={productImages[product.id]}
                        alt={product.name}
                        loading="lazy"
                        width="40"
                        height="40"
                        class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-white object-contain p-1 shrink-0"
                      />
                    )}
                    <div>
                      <h3 class="text-white font-black text-lg leading-snug m-0"><span class="block text-[#38BDF8] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 sm:hidden">{product.badge}</span>{product.name}</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">{product.category}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <span class="bg-[#38BDF8]/20 text-[#38BDF8] px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold hidden sm:block">
                    {product.badge}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-6">
